body:
That makes sense. We've also had some problems with #91172 on Windows + some Nvidia driver setups where it would crash trying to create a RenderingDevice context within an OpenGL context.

CC @clayjohn @bruvzg - sounds like we're not fully safe there on Linux too, at least with older drivers. From a quick googling of the LLVM error, it sounds like it might be caused by two libraries using LLVM at the same time in incompatible ways? In this case it could be Radeon drivers for OpenGL and Vulkan, both LLVM based I believe.

@EpicEric You should be able to work around the issue by starting the project manager with `--rendering-method forward_plus` to force using Vulkan instead of OpenGL.
